use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "All three regions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy, with error rate down to 0.002. Next I'll open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01HYZ78hLk56T2XxFcKJHxJa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.3.1-rc was only in staging and was unhealthy). The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east (us-east moved to v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west remained on v2.3.1). The rollback was retried and completed in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west, eu-west; healthy=true; error rate 0.002. No change-manager approval was needed since v2.3.0 has a healthy production history. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollout attempt.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so I'll check whether it was recorded before retrying. That avoids paging the on-call engineer twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Uaj3jGeYsUhih5hqMRvSiw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it is healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 was the unhealthy release, and v2.3.1-rc had only run in staging. Because v2.3.0 has a healthy production history, the change-manager approval policy did not apply.\n- **Rollback execution:** The first attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried the same rollback, and it completed in us-east, us-west, and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** SEV2 incident **INC-0001** is open for checkout-api. The first request to open it timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. The incident had been recorded, so I did not create a duplicate. Its summary covers the failure, the rollback, the partial first attempt, and the current state.\n\nFollow-up for the owning team: find out why v2.3.1 failed and why the first rollout attempt halted. Both are noted in the incident.", "type": "text"}]}]}